Relevant columns and their potential usage  
• USERS."created_at": user‑registration timestamp (micro‑seconds since epoch) – lets us isolate users who registered in 2019.  
• USERS."email": e‑mail address we ultimately want to list.  
• USERS."id": primary key; will join to ORDERS and ORDER_ITEMS through user_id.  

• ORDERS."created_at": order‑creation timestamp – used to keep only 2019 purchases.  
• ORDERS."user_id": foreign key back to USERS.  
• ORDERS."order_id": primary key that ties to ORDER_ITEMS.  
• ORDERS."num_of_item": number of items bought in each order (needed for order value).  

• ORDER_ITEMS."order_id": foreign key back to ORDERS.  
• ORDER_ITEMS."user_id": redundant, but handy for some joins.  
• ORDER_ITEMS."sale_price": price per item – multiplied by ORDERS."num_of_item" to get order value.  

• (Other tables are not required for this particular task.)

--------------------------------------------------------------------
Ten exploratory Snowflake queries (20‑row sample limit each)  
(All column names are enclosed in double quotes; adjust numeric timestamps / filters as you refine.)

```sql
-- 1. Quick look at 2019 user registrations (raw timestamps)
SELECT DISTINCT "id", "email", "created_at"
FROM THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.USERS
WHERE "created_at" BETWEEN 1546300800000000 AND 1577836799000000   -- 2019 calendar year
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Verify Order records that occurred in 2019
SELECT DISTINCT "order_id", "user_id", "created_at", "num_of_item"
FROM THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.ORDERS
WHERE "created_at" BETWEEN 1546300800000000 AND 1577836799000000
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Inspect Order‑Items that attach to 2019 orders
SELECT oi."order_id", oi."sale_price", o."created_at" AS "order_created_at"
FROM THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.ORDER_ITEMS oi
JOIN THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.ORDERS o
      ON oi."order_id" = o."order_id"
WHERE o."created_at" BETWEEN 1546300800000000 AND 1577836799000000
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Compute a single order’s value (num_of_item * sale_price) for 2019 orders
SELECT o."order_id",
       o."num_of_item",
       oi."sale_price",
       (o."num_of_item" * oi."sale_price") AS "order_value"
FROM THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.ORDERS o
JOIN THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.ORDER_ITEMS oi
     ON o."order_id" = oi."order_id"
WHERE o."created_at" BETWEEN 1546300800000000 AND 1577836799000000
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Aggregate total order value and total orders per user (still only 2019)
SELECT o."user_id",
       COUNT(DISTINCT o."order_id")      AS "order_cnt",
       SUM(o."num_of_item" * oi."sale_price") AS "total_sales_value"
FROM THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.ORDERS o
JOIN THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.ORDER_ITEMS oi
     ON o."order_id" = oi."order_id"
WHERE o."created_at" BETWEEN 1546300800000000 AND 1577836799000000
GROUP BY o."user_id"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Add average order value (AOV) per user for 2019
SELECT o."user_id",
       SUM(o."num_of_item" * oi."sale_price") / COUNT(DISTINCT o."order_id") AS "avg_order_value"
FROM THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.ORDERS o
JOIN THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.ORDER_ITEMS oi
     ON o."order_id" = oi."order_id"
WHERE o."created_at" BETWEEN 1546300800000000 AND 1577836799000000
GROUP BY o."user_id"
ORDER BY "avg_order_value" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7. Ensure that users in result actually registered in 2019 as well
SELECT u."id" AS "user_id",
       u."email",
       u."created_at" AS "user_created_at",
       SUM(o."num_of_item" * oi."sale_price") / COUNT(DISTINCT o."order_id") AS "avg_order_value"
FROM THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.USERS  u
JOIN THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.ORDERS o
     ON u."id" = o."user_id"
JOIN THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.ORDER_ITEMS oi
     ON o."order_id" = oi."order_id"
WHERE u."created_at" BETWEEN 1546300800000000 AND 1577836799000000   -- registered 2019
  AND o."created_at" BETWEEN 1546300800000000 AND 1577836799000000   -- purchased 2019
GROUP BY u."id", u."email", u."created_at"
ORDER BY "avg_order_value" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8. Same as #7 but pull only e‑mails (sorted by AOV)
SELECT u."email",
       SUM(o."num_of_item" * oi."sale_price") / COUNT(DISTINCT o."order_id") AS "avg_order_value"
FROM THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.USERS  u
JOIN THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.ORDERS o
     ON u."id" = o."user_id"
JOIN THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.ORDER_ITEMS oi
     ON o."order_id" = oi."order_id"
WHERE u."created_at" BETWEEN 1546300800000000 AND 1577836799000000
  AND o."created_at" BETWEEN 1546300800000000 AND 1577836799000000
GROUP BY u."email"
ORDER BY "avg_order_value" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9. Drill down to see first few 2019 high‑value customers with AOV > 50
SELECT u."email",
       SUM(o."num_of_item" * oi."sale_price") / COUNT(DISTINCT o."order_id") AS "avg_order_value"
FROM THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.USERS  u
JOIN THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.ORDERS o
     ON u."id" = o."user_id"
JOIN THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.ORDER_ITEMS oi
     ON o."order_id" = oi."order_id"
WHERE u."created_at" BETWEEN 1546300800000000 AND 1577836799000000
  AND o."created_at" BETWEEN 1546300800000000 AND 1577836799000000
GROUP BY u."email"
HAVING SUM(o."num_of_item" * oi."sale_price") / COUNT(DISTINCT o."order_id") > 50
ORDER BY "avg_order_value" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10. Final query: top‑10 emails registered & purchased in 2019 ranked by highest AOV
SELECT u."email"
FROM THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.USERS  u
JOIN THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.ORDERS o
     ON u."id" = o."user_id"
JOIN THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.ORDER_ITEMS oi
     ON o."order_id" = oi."order_id"
WHERE u."created_at" BETWEEN 1546300800000000 AND 1577836799000000
  AND o."created_at" BETWEEN 1546300800000000 AND 1577836799000000
GROUP BY u."email"
ORDER BY SUM(o."num_of_item" * oi."sale_price") / COUNT(DISTINCT o."order_id") DESC
LIMIT 10;
```

